Rebase code cache relocations to the code buffer (FEX 14c9268)

The JIT records relocation offsets relative to the temporary buffer each
block is compiled into. When generating a code cache, relocations are kept
across all compiles and serialized against the whole code buffer, so every
block after the first got its relocations applied at the first block's
offsets: the cache file held corrupted code and FEX died with SIGILL when
running from it. Rebase each compile's relocations once the block's final
location is known.

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/JIT.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/JIT.cpp
index ef7e332..a7850a5 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/JIT.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/JIT.cpp
@@ -1159,6 +1159,15 @@ CPUBackend::CompiledCode Arm64JITCore::CompileCode(uint64_t Entry, uint64_t Size
     CodeBegin += Delta;
     CodeData.HostCodeOffset = CodeData.BlockBegin - CurrentCodeBuffer->GetBufferBase();
 
+    // Relocation offsets were recorded relative to the temporary buffer. Code cache
+    // generation keeps relocations across compiles and serializes them against the
+    // whole CodeBuffer, so rebase this compile's relocations to the final location.
+    if (CTX->GetCodeCache().IsGeneratingCache) {
+      for (size_t i = PrevNumAllocations; i < Relocations.size(); ++i) {
+        Relocations[i].Header.Offset += CodeData.HostCodeOffset;
+      }
+    }
+
     // Copy over CodeBuffer contents
     memcpy(AllocatedInfo.BufferAllocationOffset, TempCodeBuffer, CodeData.Size);
   }
